0010DAr 2                       ; x = 0 repeats the last value, which is what the README documents and
0010DAr 2                       ; what Applesoft does.  msbasic builds a value out of a free-running
0010DAr 2                       ; entropy source here instead -- the Commodore behaviour -- and that
0010DAr 2                       ; was what this did: RND(0) returned neither the previous result nor
0010DAr 2                       ; anything that varied, since nothing in this machine keeps ENTROPY
0010DAr 2                       ; moving.  Every path below ends by storing the result at RNDSEED, so
0010DAr 2                       ; the last value is already there to hand back.
